2026-11-18 Deviation Investigation Kick-off Meeting (S-090 Laboratory, 6 participants) Minutes Excerpt:
1. Quality control in batch B-32386 shows a systemic trend. Among the five quality control samples from the same batch, the rate of 104.2% monotonically dropped to 79.1%, a drift of 25.1 percentage points, and the last batch has fallen below the 85% lower limit, with a coefficient of variation of 11.4% (judgment limit 3.0%);
2. Among the 96 samples to be tested in the same batch, 12 were below the lower limit of quantification, showing a significant difference compared to the previous batch's 1 sample;
3. After remelting, the actual storage of the quality control material is 5 hours and 30 minutes, with the operating procedure limited to 2 hours;
4. DEV-3034 Syringe Needle Original Factory Spare Parts Out of Supply, Replacement Parts Used for 3 Weeks.
Conclusion: Sample degradation and instrument drift cannot be distinguished; all four judgments are unacceptable. If the judgment is not accepted, the tiering table will be marked as unusable; Initiate a deviation investigation before deciding on follow-up handling. This batch will not be released, rerun, or voided for now.
Additionally: C-15030 pushed TK-20261013-5227 to first transfer to the second line; The issue of a colleague on duty taking leave until 2026-09-15 is not on this agenda. Supplementary conclusion: this case does not amount to "Open a deviation investigation".

